- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`** — `@Profile("jdbc")`, NamedParameterJdbcTemplate-based; `save` uses `SimpleJdbcInsert` for new owners.

Note: if you add a method to the `OwnerRepository` interface, all three implementations must implement it (JPA and JDBC impls implement the interface directly; only Spring Data derives methods automatically).

## 4. OwnerRequest / OwnerResponse DTOs

There are **no hand-written `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse` classes**. The DTOs are **generated at build time** by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (with suffix `Dto`). The relevant generated types used by the pipeline are:
- `OwnerFieldsDto` (request body — from schema `OwnerFields`)
- `OwnerDto` (response — from schema `Owner`)
- `OwnerPageDto`, `ValidationMessageDto` (used elsewhere)

The OpenAPI source schema (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, lines ~1991-2059):
```yaml
    OwnerFields:
      title: Owner fields
      description: Editable fields of a pet owner.
      type: object
      properties:
        firstName:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 30
          pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$"
          example: George
        lastName:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 30
          pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$"
          example: Franklin
        address:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
        city:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 80
        telephone:
          title: Telephone number
          description: >-
            The telephone number of the pet owner. On create it is normalized by
            removing every non-digit character and must be exactly 10 digits.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 20
          example: '6085551023'
      required:
        - firstName
        - lastName
        - address
        - city
        - telephone
    Owner:
      allOf:
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OwnerFields'
        - type: object
          properties:
            id:
              type: integer
              format: int32
              readOnly: true
            pets:
              type: array
              ...
```
To add request/response fields you edit `openapi.yml` (the `OwnerFields`/`Owner` schemas) and the DTOs regenerate.

## 5. Escalation YAMLs and their handlers

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`. Each YAML is just `handle: { class: <Handler> }`. Handlers live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`.

| YAML file | Handler class | Status produced |
|---|---|---|
| `...InvalidTelephoneException.yml` | `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` | 400, `errors: ["telephone"]` |
| `...MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml` | `MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` | 400, `errors: [<fields>]` |
| `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` | `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` | **404 NOT_FOUND** (note: not 409) |
| `...NotFoundException.yml` | `NotFoundExceptionHandler` | (404) |
| `java.lang.Exception.yml` | `GeneralExceptionHandler` | 500 |
| `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` | `ValidationExceptionHandler` | 400 with `schemaValidationErrors` + `errors` |
| `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` | `ForbiddenExceptionHandler` | (403) |

Key handler/exception contents:

**`InvalidTelephoneException.java`** — `extends Exception`, single-message constructor.

**`MissingOwnerFieldsException.java`** — `extends Exception`, carries `List<String> fields` with a `getFields()` accessor.

**`InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`**
```java
public void handle(@Parameter InvalidTelephoneException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>> response) {
    ProblemDetail detail = ProblemDetails.build(ex, HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
            "The request contains invalid or missing parameters");
    detail.setProperty("errors", java.util.List.of("telephone"));
    response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST).body(detail));
}
```

**`MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java`** — same shape, `detail.setProperty("errors", ex.getFields())`.

**`DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler.java`** — currently maps to `HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND` (404), not 409.

**`ProblemDetails.java`** (package-private helper) — builds the common ProblemDetail body (title = exception simple name, `timestamp`, empty `schemaValidationErrors`):
```java
static ProblemDetail build(Exception ex, HttpStatus status, String detail) {
    ProblemDetail problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatus(status);
    problemDetail.setType(URI.create("about:blank"));
    problemDetail.setTitle(ex.getClass().getSimpleName());
    problemDetail.setDetail(detail);
    problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now());
    problemDetail.setProperty("schemaValidationErrors", List.<ValidationMessageDto>of());
    return problemDetail;
}
```
`GeneralExceptionHandler` and `ValidationExceptionHandler` shown above. **There is currently NO 409/CONFLICT escalation handler** — you would need to add a new exception + handler + escalation YAML to satisfy the duplicate-telephone test (see section 7).

The escalation Java directory (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`) also contains `NotFoundException.java`, `NotFoundExceptionHandler.java`, `ForbiddenExceptionHandler.java`.

## 6. Telephone normalization / phone code

The only normalization logic is in **`BuildOwner.java`** (section 2): `request.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "")` then require length == 10, else `InvalidTelephoneException`. No other "normaliz"/"phone" helper exists.

Related telephone references:
- `Owner.java` — `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", ...)` validation.
- `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` / `InvalidTelephoneException.java` — 400 path.
- `openapi.yml` (schema doc quoted above).
- SQL schema/data: telephone column in `db/h2/schema.sql` (`telephone VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL`, **no UNIQUE constraint**), `db/hsqldb/schema.sql`, `db/mysql/schema.sql`, `db/postgres/schema.sql`, plus seed data in `db/h2/data.sql`, `db/postgres/data.sql`.
- Repository SQL `SELECT ... telephone FROM owners ...` in the JDBC impls (JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl, JdbcPetRepositoryImpl, JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl).
- Test helper `AcceptanceBase.uniqueTelephone()` → `String.format("04%08d", seq())`.

Note: the h2 schema (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql` line 37) does NOT have a UNIQUE constraint on telephone, so a duplicate-telephone rule must be enforced in application code (or by adding a DB constraint).

## 7. Tests related to creating owners

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — the target checkpoint. It expects duplicate normalized telephone to return **409 Conflict**:
```java
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone() throws Exception {
		createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
		createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}
}
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — base harness. `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(username="acceptance-admin", roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`. Key helpers:
- `ownerNode()` builds a fully-valid unique owner (firstName "Test", unique lastName/address/city/telephone).
- `createOwner(body)` → `POST /api/owners` with JSON.
- `createOwnerOk(body)` → asserts 2xx, returns id via `extractId` (reads `id` from body or `Location` header).
- `uniqueTelephone()` → `"04" + 8-digit seq` (10 digits).
- Uses Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind`).

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`** — utility to capture `AUDIT` logger events (not directly used by the current owner tests).

These three files are the entire test tree under `src/test`. So for the duplicate-telephone rule you must make `POST /api/owners` return 409 when the normalized telephone already exists (currently there is no duplicate check, no 409 handler, and no DB unique constraint).

## 8. Build file and running tests

- Build file: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`** (Maven, single module).
- Active Spring profile (default): `spring.profiles.active=h2,spring-data-jpa` in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/application.properties` — so tests run against H2 with the `SpringDataOwnerRepository` implementation.
- DTOs/APIs are generated by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (generate goal bound in build) from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (models, suffix `Dto`) and `...rest.api` (interfaces). These packages are excluded from JaCoCo coverage.
- JaCoCo `check` enforces coverage: LINE ≥ 0.85, BRANCH ≥ 0.66 (bundle level) — new code needs test coverage or the build fails.
- No explicit surefire/failsafe config; tests run via the standard `mvn test` (Surefire) using the Spring Boot parent defaults. Run: `mvn test` (or `mvn verify` to also run the JaCoCo check). To run just the acceptance test: `mvn test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.

### Summary of what an implementer needs for the duplicate-telephone (409) rule
1. Add a lookup to `OwnerRepository` (e.g. `Owner findByTelephone(String)` or a count/exists) and implement it in `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (active), plus `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` and `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` (they implement the interface directly).
2. Add the duplicate check in the POST pipeline — either inside `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` or as a new function step in `owners.POST.yml` — throwing a new checked exception (there is currently no conflict exception).
3. Add a new escalation: a `Conflict`/`DuplicateTelephoneException` class + handler returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409) + a YAML `.../escalation/<FQCN>.yml`. Note the existing `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` maps to 404, not 409, so it cannot be reused as-is.
4. Telephone must be normalized before comparison (reuse the `replaceAll("\\D","")` normalization from `BuildOwner`).

